P2-WINDOWS W7 — page:maps/NavigationRoute — WinUI 3 / Fluent parity port
========================================================================
Web source : web/src/features/maps/pages/NavigationRoutePage.tsx (route /navigation)
Output     : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/NavigationRoutePage/
             (repo convention = C#-markup feature-views, not Features/*.xaml; see sibling done pages
              RouteEfficiencyPage / TemperatureImpactPage / LocationsPage. The generated prompt's path
              apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Maps does not exist in-repo.)
Nav        : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs —
             PageFactory.Register(NavigationRouteRegistration.RouteName, static () => new FeatureViews.Maps.NavigationRoutePage())
             (RouteTable already maps Page("NavigationRoute","navigation",MapsLocation,…) at
              TeslaSync.App.Core/Navigation/RouteTable.cs:286 — no route entry added)
Strings    : every visible literal is resolved by web key through ILocalizer.GetString(key, englishFallback) in
             NavigationStrings.Resolve (Model.cs). apps/windows/Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw are catalog-
             generated (header: "AUTO-GENERATED … do not edit by hand"); the nav.* keys resolve through the
             localizer's English-fallback path, the same precedent the sibling RouteEfficiencyPage /
             TripPlannerPage follow. None hardcoded.
Units (SI) : speed_mph is m/s SI, miles_to_arrival is metres SI (Phase-48). Converted at the display boundary only
             via UnitConverters.SpeedFromSi / DistanceFromSi + UnitLabels (Model.cs). No non-SI stored/computed.

Data sources (web hooks ported, same names at the C# call sites):
  useChargingTelemetryLatest  GET /charging-telemetry/latest [vehicle_id]  -> Operations.Charging.TelemetryLatest
  useLocationSnapshotLatest   GET /location-snapshots/latest [vehicle_id]  -> Operations.Locations.SnapshotLatest
  useLocationSnapshots        GET /location-snapshots [vehicle_id,limit]   -> Operations.Locations.SnapshotHistory (added)
  (NavigationRouteClientFeed: latest = primary/error-propagating; history + charging = best-effort/degrade.)

Files:
  feature-views/NavigationRoutePage/NavigationRoutePage.Model.cs      (parsers + snapshot + feed iface + EmptyFeed + display records + NavigationStrings(60) + projection + registration + diagnostics)
  feature-views/NavigationRoutePage/NavigationRoutePage.Source.cs     (generated C# client GET adapter: NavigationRouteClientFeed — 3 reads)
  feature-views/NavigationRoutePage/NavigationRoutePage.ViewModel.cs  (INotifyPropertyChanged data holder + state matrix + units + freshness flags)
  feature-views/NavigationRoutePage/NavigationRoutePage.cs            (WinUI 3 UserControl, Fluent + design tokens + AutomationPeer)
  TeslaSync.App.Core/Data/Net/Operations.cs                          (+Locations.SnapshotHistory = get_api_v1_location_snapshots)
  TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs                             (PageFactory registration)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/NavigationRoutePageTests.cs        (53 headless tests)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj                      (link the 3 UI-free files; the WinUI view is build-only)

